Modern mingw-w64 provides TOUCHINPUT (with _WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0601);
Qt 5.9's local fallback definition guarded on Q_CC_MINGW then collides.
Only fall back when the SDK really lacks the touch API.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsmousehandler.cpp
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsmousehandler.cpp
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@
  * are present in the Windows SDK's, but not in older MSVC Express
  * versions. */
 
-#if defined(Q_CC_MINGW) || !defined(TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE)
+#if !defined(TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE)
 
 typedef struct tagTOUCHINPUT {
     LONG x;
